# Optional. Set this to enable the AI-powered chat assistant on the
# Contact page (natural-language product suggestions + store info).
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/
#
# If this is left unset, the chat assistant still works using a built-in
# rule-based fallback (keyword matching against the product catalog) —
# no key required.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your key, then restart the server.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Set this to enable "Sign in with Google" on the login page.
#
# How to get one:
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   2. Create (or pick) a project, then "Create Credentials" -> "OAuth client ID"
#   3. Application type: "Web application"
#   4. Under "Authorized JavaScript origins" add the URL(s) you serve the
#      site from, e.g. http://localhost:3000 and your production domain
#   5. Copy the generated Client ID (looks like xxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com)
#      into GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID below
#
# No client secret is needed — Google Sign-In here uses Google Identity
# Services (a client-side button that returns a verified ID token), and the
# server only verifies that token. If this is left unset, the Google button
# simply doesn't appear and email/password login keeps working as normal.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional. Set both of these to enable "Continue with Facebook" on the
# login page.
#
# How to get them:
#   1. Go to https://developers.facebook.com/apps and create an app
#      (choose "Consumer" as the app type)
#   2. Add the "Facebook Login" product to the app
#   3. Under Facebook Login -> Settings, add the URL(s) you serve the site
#      from to "Valid OAuth Redirect URIs" / "Allowed Domains for the JS
#      SDK", e.g. http://localhost:3000 and your production domain
#   4. Find your App ID and App Secret under Settings -> Basic
#   5. Copy them into FACEBOOK_APP_ID / FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET below
#
# The frontend uses the Facebook JS SDK (a client-side button that returns
# a short-lived user access token), and the server verifies that token
# with Facebook using the App Secret before creating/logging in the
# account — the secret never reaches the browser. If either value is left
# unset, the Facebook button simply doesn't appear and the rest of login
# keeps working as normal.
FACEBOOK_APP_ID=
FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET=

# Optional. Where product/order/theme JSON data and uploaded images are
# stored on disk. Leave unset for local development (defaults to ./data
# and ./public/uploads inside the project folder).
#
# ON RENDER: the default web service filesystem is EPHEMERAL — every
# restart/redeploy/sleep-wake cycle wipes it, which resets your products,
# orders, and theme edits. To fix this, add a "Persistent Disk" to your
# Render service (Settings -> Disks -> Add Disk), e.g. mounted at
# /var/data, then set:
#   DATA_DIR=/var/data/data
#   UPLOADS_DIR=/var/data/uploads
# The server will automatically create these folders and seed them with
# default data the first time (existing data is never overwritten).
# Note: Persistent Disks require a paid Render instance type (not
# available on the free plan).
DATA_DIR=
UPLOADS_DIR=
